# The supersingular estimate in terms of actual geometric kernels

The prime-to-characteristic factor hypotheses ensure that kernel cardinalities
are degrees. The order-six subgroup is generated by the specified actual point.
No CM actions, common roots, or matching quadratic polynomials are assumed.
